@100  = ~Jarnip: A New Bonus Merchant in the Adventurer's Mart~
@101  = ~Must be installed on BG2EE or EET~
@102  = ~Jarnip~
@103  = ~Jarnip's Wares~
@104  = ~Heart of Fury +3~
@105  = ~This impressive two-handed sword originally belonged to the Tribe of the Great White Wyrm, a barbarian clan from Icewind Dale that worshipped the white dragon matriarch Icasaracht. After Icasaracht was slain by a group of adventurers, the clan scattered, and its heirloom fell into the hands of outsiders. Despite the passage of time, the sword has retained Icasaracht's enchantment, and you can feel it pulsing with cold, primal fury.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Physical Damage Resistance: +20%
– Hit Points: +15 (Barbarians)

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d10+3 (slashing), +1 (cold)
Speed Factor: 7
Proficiency Type: Two-Handed Sword
Type: Two-Handed
Requires:
15 Strength

Weight: 10~
@106  = ~Gilded Bulwark +2~
@107  = ~This armor was commissioned at great expense by Sir Alrond, a wealthy nobleman from Athkatla who bribed his way into the ranks of the Order of the Radiant Heart. Eager to flaunt his newly acquired title, Alrond ordered an extraordinary suit of armor that no other knight could match. The result is indeed a masterpiece: ornate, intricate, and gleaming, this armor is virtually immune to enemy blows. Unfortunately, due to its complexity, it was also too heavy for Alrond to wear. Humiliated and financially ruined, he was forced to sell the plate and was shortly after slain by a gibberling. Though it reeks of vanity, this armor offers exceptional protection, provided its new owner has the strength to wear it.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Physical Damage Resistance: +5% (+15% for Cavaliers)
– Charisma: +1 (+2 for Cavaliers)

Armor Class: -1 (-5 vs. slashing, -4 vs. piercing and missile), -2 (Cavaliers)
Requires:
 18 Strength

Weight: 100~
@108  = ~Elaine +3~
@109  = ~This longbow is a masterpiece of Elven craftsmanship. It once belonged to Elaine, a legendary Arcane Archer who fell defending the elven city of Askavar over a thousand years ago. Some claim that Elaine's soul still resides within the bow, empowering its arrows with magical energy. Only those of Elven heritage may use it.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– +2 THAC0 and damage, +1 attack speed factor (Fighter/Mages only)

Combat abilities:
– When no arrows are equipped, the bow fires missiles that are treated as +3 for the purposes of determining what enemies they can damage. The missiles receive +3 to hit and deal 1d6 missile and 1d3 magic damage

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d6 (missile), +1d3 (magic)
Speed Factor: 4
Proficiency Type: Longbow
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 10 Strength
 13 Intelligence

Weight: 3~
@110  = ~Moonshade +3~
@111  = ~Moonblades are magical longswords that were forged in ancient Myth Drannor. They are immensely valuable to the elves and are used in the long process of selecting a ruler for the isle of Evermeet. Normally, a moonblade chooses its owner, but this particular sword seems willing to be wielded by anyone of elven heritage. It retains a powerful enchantment that greatly improves its wielder's arcane and martial abilities.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +1
– Spell Casting Speed: +2

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d8+3 (slashing), +1 (magic)
Speed Factor: 2
Proficiency Type: Longsword
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 10 Strength
 13 Intelligence

Weight: 3~
@112  = ~Bloodstone Ranger's Hood~
@113  = ~This hood was crafted by the Wardens of the Bloodstone Gate, an elite circle of rangers who once patrolled the mountain passes of Damara. It is said that this hood sharpens the senses of its wearer, enabling them to detect danger from a safe distance and strike first.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Weapon Speed Factor: +1
– Visual Range: +2 (+4 for Stalkers)
– Attacks per round: +1/2 (Stalkers)
– Protects against critical hits

Weight: 2~
@114  = ~Herbert's Rapier +2~
@115  = ~The rapier is a light, thrusting sword often associated with nobles, duelists, and swashbucklers. It is not a popular weapon in Baldur's Gate and Amn, where broader and heavier blades are preferred. This particular rapier once belonged to Herbert Schwarz, a renowned Waterdhavian duelist who famously won twenty-one duels against heavily armored knights without ever wearing armor himself.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +2
– Critical Hit chance: +5% (Swashbucklers and Blades)
– Luck: +1 (Swashbucklers)

Combat abilities:
– On hit: improves the wielder's Armor Class by 1 for 2 rounds

THAC0: +2
Damage: 1d6+2 (piercing)
Speed Factor: 1
Proficiency Type: Longsword
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 5 Strength
 14 Dexterity

Weight: 2~
@116  = ~The Weavebreaker~
@117  = ~This amulet is forged from a strange metal that seems to absorb any magical energy in its vicinity. Wizards standing nearby often describe an oppressive sensation, as though the Weave itself grows thin in the amulet's presence. Because this amulet owes its properties not to enchantment but to the properties of the mysterious ore, it is one of the few magic items that Wizard Slayers can use.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Save vs. Spell: +1 (+2 for Wizard Slayers)
– Magic Resistance: +5% (+10% for Wizard Slayers)
– Disables the use of arcane spells by the wearer
– Can be worn by Wizard Slayers

Combat abilities:
– Enemies within 30 ft. suffer 25% arcane spell failure (Wizard Slayers)

Weight: 2~
@118  = ~Eye of the Storm +3~
@119  = ~This obsidian spear is adorned with the symbol of Talos etched just beneath its head. It likely belonged to a senior Talassan stormlord, as its single swing can summon terrifying thunder and rain. You can feel the air electrifying when you hold this fearsome weapon, but its true wrath is only unleashed in battle.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Electricity Damage: +15% (Druids)

Combat abilities:
– On hit: 15% chance to cast Call Lightning on the target (4d8 damage, save vs. spell for half)
– Attacks change local weather to thunderstorm

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d8+3 (piercing), +1d4 (electrical)
Speed Factor: 3
Proficiency Type: Spear
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 6 Strength
 12 Wisdom

Weight: 5~
@120  = ~Circlet of the Drunken Master~
@121  = ~The Way of the Drunken Master is a monastic tradition that teaches its practitioners to relinquish control over their bodies and become one with alcoholic beverages. While their clumsy fighting style may appear unskilled, it actually conceals exceptionally precise movements that almost always catch opponents off guard. The followers of the Way of the Drunken Master spend most of their time in taverns, yet this magical circlet puts its wearer in a blissful state of alcoholic intoxication without any of the usual downsides.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Protects against critical hits
– The wearer is under a permanent state of magical alcohol intoxication. It grants +3 to Armor Class and +1 to THAC0 and Damage when attacking with fists. It has no negative impact on Luck or Saving Throws (Monks)

Weight: 3~
@122  = ~Judicator +3~
@123  = ~According to legends, Judicator was forged by archons of Mount Celestia and bestowed upon a mortal Justiciar of Tyr centuries ago. Since then, it has assisted innumerable battles against the forces of evil, even beyond Toril. Judicator shines with a divine light that blazes upon its foes, blinding the unworthy and smiting evil with holy radiance.

STATISTICS:

Combat abilities:
– On hit: The target must Save vs. Spell or become blinded for 1 round
– On hit: 15% chance of casting Holy Smite centered on the target: affects evil only, 6d4 damage, save vs. spell for half

THAC0: +3
Damage: 2d4+4 (crushing), +3 vs. evil (magic)
Speed Factor: 1
Proficiency Type: War Hammer
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 9 Strength
 13 Wisdom

Weight: 6~
@124  = ~Kensai's Arm +2~
@125  = ~The blade of this katana is forged from a rippling, wave-patterned steel. It is so sharp that it can slice through a single strand of hair. Crafting a weapon of this quality clearly required meticulous effort and time, but its true power lies in the soul of the Kensai bound within. If the spirit senses that the wielder also follows the path of the Sword Saint, it awakens and helps to guide their arm.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Attacks per round: +1/2 (+1 for Kensai)

Combat abilities:
– For 10 seconds after activating Kai, the chance to score a critical hit increases by 10% (Kensai)

THAC0: +2
Damage: 1d10+2 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 2
Proficiency Type: Katana
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 6 Strength

Weight: 5~
@126  = ~Obsidian Splint Mail +3~
@127  = ~This suit of splint mail is unlike any forged from ordinary iron or steel. Each interlocking plate has been painstakingly crafted from obsidian crystal, polished until it gleams in the dark. Though heavier than most armors of its kind, it offers formidable resistance to magic.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Magic Resistance: +10% (+20% for Wizard Slayers)
– Saving Throws: +1 (+2 for Wizard Slayers)

Armor Class: 1 (0 vs. piercing and missile, -1 vs. crushing)
Requires:
 15 Strength

Weight: 50~
@128  = ~Reghedmen Iron Circlet~
@129  = ~This bare iron band was the war-helm of one of the barbarian chieftains from the Reghed Glacier who led the failed assault on the Ten Towns centuries ago. Said to be quenched in the blood of fallen foes and blessed by Tempus, this circlet sharpens the senses in the heat of battle, allowing its wearer to strike with deadly rage.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– THAC0 and Damage: +1
– Hit Points: +10
– Each time the wearer is hit in combat, Slashing, Crushing, and Piercing Damage increases by further 5% for 1 round (Barbarians)
– Protects against critical hits

Weight: 1~
@130  = ~Iron Resolve +2~
@131  = ~The blade of this sword is plain and unremarkable, forged from dark, unpolished iron. Its worn grip and nicked blade suggest that it has seen countless battles. Though lacking ornament, the sword is exceptionally well balanced and is said to answer to the resolve of its wielder.

STATISTICS: 

Equipped abilities:
– When Hit Points fall below 50%, the wielder gains +2 bonus to THAC0. When Hit Points fall below 25%, the wielder gains an additional +2 THAC0 bonus and a +5% bonus to Critical Hit chance (Fighters)

Combat abilities:
– On hit: 20% chance to grant the wielder +1 bonus to damage for 1 turn

THAC0: +2
Damage: 2d4+2 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 5
Proficiency Type: Bastard Sword
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 11 Strength

Weight: 7~
@132  = ~Bloodlust +5~
@133  = ~Cursed Berserking Sword +5: Bloodlust

Waterdhavian parents often tell their children the tale of Bloodlust: a cursed berserking sword with an insatiable desire to murder that ultimately turns on its wielder to quench its thirst for blood. The moral of the story is to never accept unknown magical items from strangers, and the sword was thought to be nothing more than a legend. However, it now lies before you.

The crimson blade is covered in bloodmarks, suggesting it is hundreds of years old. If the legends are true, it has caused the death of thousands, and countless innocents have fallen victim to its malevolent influence. The origins of Bloodlust are unclear, but it is evident that it was created for one purpose: to kill without end and unleash carnage across the Realms. 

The curse of this sword permanently marks the wielder: their hair turns white and begins to fall out, while their skin becomes ghastly and riddled with blisters. Over time, they lose physical fortitude and wither from within. The only way to alleviate this affliction is through satiating the blade's desire for bloodshed, yet the curse itself may never be lifted.

Once equipped, this cursed sword cannot be removed or unequipped by any known spell or ritual. The wielder has no choice but to obey and continue the slaughter. Only death can grant freedom from its curse.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Cursed
– Immune to Remove Curse
– Charisma: -5 penalty
– Constitution: -2 penalty
– Appearance changes: skin turns pale gray, hair becomes bone-white

Combat abilities:
– Murderous Wrath: On each hit, the wielder must Save vs. Death or go berserk for 2 rounds. When berserk, the movement rate is doubled and the base number of attacks per round is set to 5
– Dread Hunger: On each hit, the target must Save vs. Death or receive extra 2d4 magic damage. The stolen Hit Points are transferred to the wielder. This will not heal beyond the wielder's maximum
– Bloodlust: Killing an enemy restores 4d6 Hit Points and increases Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution by 1 for 1 turn

THAC0: +5
Damage: 2d4+5 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 3
Proficiency Type: Bastard Sword
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 10 Strength

Weight: 10~
@134  = ~Korgunth's Right Fist +2~
@135  = ~This heavy stone hammer once belonged to Korgunth Ironwarden, a dwarven defender from the Silver Marches. Unlike most dwarven defenders, Korgunth favored an aggressive two-weapon fighting style, charging into enemy ranks with rage. Due to its sheer weight, his hammer, known as the "Right Fist," was capable of delivering devastating blows, especially against the traditional enemies of the dwarves: goblins, orcs, and giants.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Resistance to Slashing, Piercing, and Crushing Damage: +5%
– Strength: +1 (Dwarves)

THAC0: +2
Damage: 2d4+3 (crushing), extra 2d4+3 vs. goblins, orcs, and giants
Speed Factor: 2
Proficiency Type: War Hammer
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 17 Strength

Weight: 20~
@136  = ~Korgunth's Left Fist +2~
@137  = ~This heavy stone hammer once belonged to Korgunth Ironwarden, a dwarven defender from the Silver Marches. Unlike most dwarven defenders, Korgunth favored an aggressive two-weapon fighting style, charging into enemy ranks with rage. The "Left Fist" was essential to Korgunth's martial techniques and allowed him to strike with deadly swiftness.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Resistance to Slashing, Piercing, and Crushing Damage: +5%
– Constitution: +1
– Attacks per round: +1/2 (Dwarven Defenders)

THAC0: +2
Damage: 2d4+3 (crushing)
Speed Factor: 2
Proficiency Type: War Hammer
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 17 Strength

Weight: 20~
@138  = ~Silver Watch +2~
@139  = ~The blade of this finely decorated halberd has gold-plated edges and is forged from shiny, polished steel. It was commissioned by the Grand Dukes of Baldur's Gate for the captain of the Flaming Fist's Honor Guard. Although forged for ceremonial purposes, the halberd is also lethal in combat. Its unusually long shaft and spike at the top allow the wielder to keep enemies at bay and stagger them with precise strikes. It is a beautiful weapon, equally suited for the battlefield and grand military parades.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Movement Rate: +2 (Fighters)

Combat abilities:
– Melee range increased by 50% (3 ft. total)
– On hit: 33% chance to stagger the target in place for 1 round (no save)

THAC0: +2
Damage: 1d10+2 (slashing or piercing, whichever is better)
Speed Factor: 7
Proficiency Type: Halberd
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 15 Strength
 12 Dexterity

Weight: 12~
@140  = ~Black Doom +2~
@141  = ~At first glance, this blackened iron shield seems old and unremarkable. However, upon closer inspection, you notice a faint symbol of Bane carved on its interior. It once belonged to a forsaken Blackguard who ravaged the coast of Tethyr during one of its civil wars. Ultimately, the Banite was hunted down by the Loyal Order of Innocents, and his name was erased from recorded history.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +3 (+5 for Blackguards)
– Saving Throws: +1 (+3 for Blackguards)

Combat abilities:
– Casts Doom on whoever hits the wielder: -2 penalty to THAC0 and Saving Throws for 1 turn

Requires:
 9 Strength~
@142  = ~Herbert's Black Mantle~
@143  = ~Herbert Schwarz was a famous Waterdhavian duelist whose adventures along the Sword Coast left behind as many tavern brawls as humiliated opponents. It is said that nearly every inn between Waterdeep and Baldur's Gate eventually displayed a notice declaring that the adventurer was no longer a welcome guest. Whether he departed on his own or was driven by a coalition of organized innkeepers, the tales claim Herbert eventually wandered south in search of new adventures.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +1
– Melee THAC0: +1 (+2 for Swashbucklers and Blades)
– Melee Critical Hit chance: +5% (Swashbucklers and Blades)

Weight: 2~
@144  = ~Helm of the Faithful~
@145  = ~A relic of the Lathanderite church, Helm of the Faithful is said to be imbued with the divine essence of the "Armor of Faith" spell. While the protection it provides may appear modest, any experienced knight will immediately recognize its value, especially on the most perilous journeys.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Resistance to all damage types: +5% (Paladins and Clerics)
– Armor Class: +1
– Saving Throws: +1   
– Protects against critical hits

Weight: 2~
@146  = ~Wayfarer +4~
@147  = ~This leather armor was crafted for the leader of the Wardens of the Bloodstone Gate, an elite circle of rangers who once patrolled the mountain passes of Damara. The group was known for their ambush tactics, and its equipment was specifically crafted to support long mountainous journeys. This armor is decorated with fox fur and surprisingly lightweight, enabling its wearer to attack swiftly and disappear immediately afterwards.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Movement Rate: +2
– Immunity to fatigue
– Backstab Multiplier: +1 (Stalkers)

Armor Class: 3 (1 vs. slashing, 2 vs. piercing and missile), 2 (Stalkers)
Requires:
 3 Strength

Weight: 3~
@148  = ~Slayer of Men +2~
@149  = ~When the first settlements of the Ten Towns were established some three hundred years ago, the barbarian clans vowed to drive the so-called "civilized" men from their ancestral lands. They soon launched a brutal campaign, conducting devastating raids on neighboring towns. It is said that one of the barbarian chieftains was capable of cleaving through multiple foes with a single swing of his two-handed axe, which soon became known as the "Slayer of Men." The bloodstains on its blade serve as a vivid reminder of this violent period in Icewind Dale's history.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: -2 Penalty
– Attacks per round: +1/2 (Berserkers and Barbarians)

Combat abilities:
– On hit: The target must save vs. Death or fall on the ground for 1 round
– Cleave: 33% chance on hit to deal an additional 1d12+2 slashing damage to all enemies within 3 ft. in front of the wielder

THAC0: +2
Damage: 1d12+2 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 7
Proficiency Type: Axe
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 16 Strength

Weight: 15~
@150  = ~Tormish Gauntlets~
@151  = ~On rare occasions, gauntlets such as these are granted to champions of Torm after they have distinguished themselves in the service of the Church. They are trimmed with silver and designed to closely resemble Torm's holy symbol, making them immediately recognizable to all followers of the God of Duty.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +1
– Saving Throws: +1
– Spell Casting Speed: +1 (Clerics and Paladins)
– Divine Casting Level: +1 (Clerics and Paladins)

Weight: 1~
@200  = ~Jarnip in ToB: A New Merchant in Saradush~
@201  = ~Must be installed on BG2EE or EET~
@202  = ~Jarnip~
@203  = ~Jarnip's Wares~
@204  = ~Bane of the Innocent +4~
@205  = ~The first victims of this sword were not knights. They were pilgrims. Peasants. Beggars. Those who could not fight back.

Long ago, this forsaken blade belonged to an unnamed holy champion who was suddenly stripped of his deity's grace. Instead of seeking penance, he chose the path of vengeance. It is said that the slaughter of the followers of his former faith was so great that the screams of his victims became permanently imbued within the blade.

Bane of the Innocent strikes terror into the hearts of those who face it and does not tolerate the touch of the righteous. Because of unspeakable atrocities committed with it in the past, only Blackguards and fallen paladins can wield it.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Fire Resistance: +30%
– Characters of Good or Neutral alignment are slain upon equipping this sword

Combat abilities:
– Touch of Terror: 25% chance on hit to cause the target to panic for 4 rounds
– Dooming Presence: 5% chance on hit that all enemies within a 15-ft. radius panic and receive a -2 penalty to Armor Class, hit rolls, and damage rolls for 1 turn

THAC0: +4 
Damage: 2d4+4 (slashing), +2d4 (fire)
Speed Factor: 4 
Proficiency Type: Bastard Sword
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 10 Strength

Weight: 3~
@206  = ~The Triumphant +5~
@207  = ~According to legend, the Triumphant first belonged to a barbarian king of Narfell who perished while defending his homeland from an invading horde from the Endless Wastes. The sword was said to have been found on the battlefield after its wielder had single-handedly defeated an entire army. No body was ever found. Only the sword remained, lying amid the dead.

Since that time, the Triumphant has appeared in countless sagas of the northern barbarian tribes, becoming a symbol of might and perseverance. Some say that whoever claims the sword is destined for greatness, while others believe that the blade simply finds those who are worthy of it.

Whatever the truth, those who take up the Triumphant soon discover that even impossible odds can be overcome.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Strength: +1
– Constitution: +1

Combat abilities:
– Heroic Inspiration: While enraged, increases Armor Class by 2, Critical Hit chance by 5%, and grants an extra attack per round
– Furious Strikes: On a critical hit, the target is knocked back for 1 round

THAC0: +5
Damage: 1d10+5 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 5
Proficiency Type: Two-handed Sword
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 16 Strength

Weight: 15~
@208  = ~Harper's Gift +3~
@209  = ~This richly adorned off-hand dagger bears the crest of the Harpers and has a large sapphire set into its pommel. It originally belonged to Elminster Aumar, who gifted it to an unnamed Harper agent tasked with infiltrating the Zhentil Keep from within. Although the fate of the Harper remains unknown, the dagger has somehow found its way back to the Sword Coast.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +2
– Attacks per round: +1 (Bards and Thieves)

Combat abilities:
– Sapphire Guard: On a critical miss, casts Mirror Image on self

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d4+3 (piercing)
Speed Factor: 0
Proficiency Type: Dagger
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 3 Strength

Weight: 1~
@210  = ~Watcher's Oath +3~
@211  = ~Holy Shield of Protection: Watcher's Oath

Once, Watcher's Oath was a simple, unenchanted shield that belonged to a nameless Helmite squire. The young knight fell while protecting his comrades during a siege of Helm's Hold, and his shield was shattered in battle. In honor of his sacrifice, the Helmites reforged the shield so that it might serve as a symbol of unwavering duty. Its newly crafted rim is intricately decorated and features an engraved prayer to the Vigilant One, requesting aid for its bearer and all those who stand beside them.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +4
– Saving Throws: +2
– Aura of Protection: All party members gain +1 to Armor Class and +1 to all Saving Throws (Paladins)

Requires:
 10 Strength
 13 Wisdom

Weight: 8~
@212  = ~Pride of Ammarindar +4~
@213  = ~Weapons such as this two-handed axe were granted to dwarven elders in ancient Ammarindar when they were chosen to lead their clans. Its blade is made from mithral steel and adorned with dwarven runes that speak of loyalty toward one's clan and kingdom. The few surviving weapons are exceptionally rare and held in great reverence among the dwarves.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Saving Throws: +1 (+2 for Dwarven Defenders)
- Physical Damage Resistance: +10% (+20% for Dwarven Defenders)

Combat abilities:
- Unyielding Assault: Each hit heals the wielder for 4 Hit Points. This will not heal beyond the wielder's maximum
- Crushing Blow: 25% chance on hit to reduce the target's Armor Class by 2 for 4 rounds

THAC0: +4
Damage: 1d10+4 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 5
Proficiency Type: Axe
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 15 Strength

Weight: 15~
@214  = ~Grace of Eldath +5~
@215  = ~During one of the wars between Rashemen and Thay, a young vychlaran found herself trapped in Ashenwood, being pursued by Thayan mercenaries. When all hope seemed lost, she noticed a green, feminine hand emerging from a nearby pond, holding what appeared to be a wooden branch. The branch turned out to be a unique Staff of the Woodlands, which enabled her to escape her pursuers and safely return to Mulsantir. Whether the legend is true or not, this staff is said to be blessed by the Green Goddess herself and invoke her judgment against anyone who dares to harm the druid wielding it.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Fire and Cold Resistance: +20%
– Armor Class: +1
– Saving Throws: +1
– Wisdom: +2

Combat abilities:
– Emerald Rebuke: Any creature that strikes the wielder in melee must save vs. Staff at -2 or suffer 1d10+5 poison damage and become entangled for 4 rounds (Druids)

THAC0: +5
Damage: 1d6+5 (crushing)
Speed Factor: 0
Proficiency Type: Quarterstaff
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 10 Dexterity
 15 Wisdom

Weight: 4~
@216  = ~Helm of the High Inquisitor~
@217  = ~The legendary Tyrian inquisitor Adsiltia wore this enchanted helmet during her final battle, when she descended into Cania to rescue her betrothed from the clutches of Mephistopheles. The outcome of their confrontation remains unknown, but somehow the helmet survived and eventually found its way back to Toril.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +1
– Saving Throws: +1 (+2 for Inquisitors)
– Magic Resistance: +5% (+10% for Inquisitors)

Combat abilities:
– Aura of Judgment: Enemies within 30 ft. cast spells at +2 casting time (Inquisitor only)

Weight: 5~
@218  = ~Cloak of the Scarlet Abbot~
@219  = ~Long ago, this cloak was a hereditary artifact worn by the abbots of the Monastery of the Scarlet Rose in Shou Lung. After the monastery was raided and destroyed by the Tuigan Horde, the artifact was thought lost forever. How it eventually found its way to the Sword Coast remains unknown.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Hit Points: +10
– Attacks per round: +1 (Monks)

Combat abilities:
– Scarlet Palm: Each successful melee hit with fists has a 25% chance to stun the target for 1 round (save vs. Spell negates)

Weight: 4~
@220  = ~Robe of Balagos~
@221  = ~This opulent robe was crafted by the red dragon Balagos for his use whenever he assumed a human form. He later gifted it to a group of his human worshippers as a reward for their service. Woven from heavy Calimshan silk and adorned with the scales of a great wyrm, the robe still channels Balagos's power and is said to recognize those of draconic blood.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: 4
– Spell Casting Speed: +2
– Physical Damage Resistance: +25% (Red Dragon Disciples)
– Fire Damage dealt by the wearer: +20% (Red Dragon Disciples)

Charge abilities:
– Casts Dragon Breath once per day
 Damage: 20d10 (Save vs. Breath for half)
 Area: 15-ft. radius
 Does not harm party members

Weight: 3~
@222  = ~Dance of Death +3~
@223  = ~Few know the true name of the assassin who committed a series of murders targeting high-profile figures in Athkatla some fifty years ago. The surviving accounts call her only the Dancer, a master of stealth who could slip through crowded streets and guarded halls without ever being seen. It is said that she served no lord and accepted no payment, targeting wealthy slavers and corrupt officials according to her own sense of justice. After her final assassination of a high-ranking Cowled Wizard, the Dancer was nearly captured but managed to escape, leaving behind only her blade.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Backstab Multiplier: -1 penalty
– Non-detection

