@224  = ~Herbert's Coat +5~
@225  = ~This exceptional leather coat once belonged to Herbert Schwarz, a famous Waterdhavian duelist whose adventures along the Sword Coast became the subject of innumerable folk tales. Herbert was known for being able to escape from even the most dangerous situations, a talent many attributed to his magic armor. Durable, comfortable, and enchanted with a permanent blessing of fortune, this coat is the dream of any adventurer.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Saving Throws: +1
– Luck: +1 (Swashbucklers)

Combat abilities:
– Avoid Death: When the wearer's Hit Points fall below 10%, grants 15 temporary hit points, +4 to Armor Class, and +4 to Saving Throws for 1 round

Armor Class: 2 (0 vs. slashing, 1 vs. piercing and missile), 0 (Swashbucklers)
Requires:
 8 Strength

Weight: 10~
@226  = ~Scourge of the Sky +3~
@227  = ~Scourge of the Sky is said to have originally belonged to an ancient Tuigan hero who united the fifteen tribes of the Endless Wastes for the first time. Since then, it has passed down through numerous warlords who sought to become the next Khan. Clearly intended only for the most formidable Tuigan archers, this composite longbow is exceptionally sturdy and demands both great strength and skill to wield effectively.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Three shots per round (Archers), one shot per round (others)

Combat abilities:
– The bow fires missiles that are treated as +3 for the purposes of determining what enemies they can damage. The missiles receive +4 to hit and deal 1d6+2 missile damage

THAC0: +4
Damage: 1d6+2 (missile)
Speed Factor: 4
Proficiency Type: Longbow
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 19 Strength

Weight: 8~
